     "rate": "+0%",
     "text": "In nineteen eighty-four, Marvel Comics put every hero and villain onto a fabricated planet called Battleworld. You think crossover fiction stays on the page, but that twelve issue series mirrored real proxy battles. Max Hastings noted that intelligence and secret operations became a major growth industry during World War Two. So nations constantly ran covert operations behind the scenes, and readers watched those hidden themes play out. Ronald Reagan was running a secret war, quietly selling arms to Iran to fund rebel forces. The series ran from May nineteen eighty-four to April nineteen eighty-five, matching that exact era. Fiction exposes the quiet anxieties of its time, turning real political proxies into cosmic battles."
    }
   }
